{"title":"Career Roadmap · GIS Planner","role":"GIS Planner","summary":"A GIS Planner uses Geographic Information Systems, spatial data, mapping, remote sensing, planning analytics, and geospatial modelling to support decisions about land use, transportation, infrastructure, housing, landscape, environment, and urban development.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Plan (Bachelor of Planning)","Course":"Landscape / Transport / Infrastructure Planning"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A GIS Planner uses Geographic Information Systems, spatial data, mapping, remote sensing, planning analytics, and geospatial modelling to support decisions about land use, transportation, infrastructure, housing, landscape, environment, and urban development."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Plan student specializing in Landscape / Transport / Infrastructure Planning, GIS is particularly valuable because almost every planning decision has a spatial component."},{"type":"p","text":"A GIS Planner may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Land-use and zoning analysis"},{"text":"Transportation and accessibility planning"},{"text":"Infrastructure mapping"},{"text":"Urban growth analysis"},{"text":"Landscape and environmental planning"},{"text":"Housing and development suitability"},{"text":"Utility and public-service mapping"},{"text":"Disaster and climate-risk mapping"},{"text":"Smart-city projects"},{"text":"Regional planning"},{"text":"Site selection and feasibility studies"},{"text":"Urban analytics and spatial modelling"},{"text":"GIS-based decision-support systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Urban/Infrastructure Planning","GIS","Spatial Analytics","Remote Sensing","Python/SQL","Transport/Landscape Knowledge"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Plan Student"},{"text":"Planning + GIS + spatial analysis"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"GIS Planner / GIS Analyst"},{"text":"Mapping, spatial analysis, planning projects"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior GIS Planner / Spatial Planning Specialist"},{"text":"Advanced modelling, infrastructure & urban analytics"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"GIS Planning Lead / Geospatial Strategy Consultant"},{"text":"Large-scale planning, GIS strategy, digital cities"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Plan","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Planning + Spatial Thinking"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong planning fundamentals before becoming tool-dependent."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urban and regional planning"},{"text":"Human settlements"},{"text":"Urban geography"},{"text":"Demography"},{"text":"Land-use planning"},{"text":"Housing"},{"text":"Transportation planning"},{"text":"Infrastructure planning"},{"text":"Environmental planning"},{"text":"Landscape planning"},{"text":"Urban economics"},{"text":"Planning theory"},{"text":"Development regulations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Spatial concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Density"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Connectivity"},{"text":"Proximity"},{"text":"Catchment areas"},{"text":"Land-use relationships"},{"text":"Urban morphology"},{"text":"Spatial distribution"},{"text":"Urban growth patterns"},{"text":"The goal is to understand why a spatial pattern exists, not simply how to draw it on a map."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — GIS Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important technical stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn GIS systematically"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS Pro"},{"text":"OpenStreetMap"},{"text":"Google Earth